Constrain each batched request with its own answer space

The batched call built one SamplingParams with a nested choice list - one
candidate list per request - which pydantic rejected outright: choice is a flat
list of strings. Fixing the shape alone would still have been wrong, because a
shared constraint would let a single-choice item emit an ordered multi-select
sequence from another request's space.

Build one SamplingParams per request and pass the sequence to engine.chat, which
pairs parameters with prompts one by one. Add a test that drives generate_batch
with a single-choice item and an ordered multi-select in the same batch and
asserts each request receives its own choice list with flat string entries;
confirmed it fails against the shared-constraint code.

Package digests change; re-run the packaging command to obtain the new
manifest_sha256.
